        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0390" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg348"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extracts.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 441.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 1, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit, out of the ordinary course, a
                    report of the proceedings in the House of Commons last night, on the motion made
                    by Mr. Roebuck. It is difficult to imagine a more awkward situation than that in
                    which he has succeeded in placing as well his own government as the Emperor of
                    the French.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
